WEBVTT

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:33.760
Okay, go!

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.930
Got it!

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.830
This woman is...

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.120
Yes.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.660
Princess Cybele of the Pulizia Monarchy.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.330
She was pretty hot, Miss New Editor.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.090
But I'm amazed you have a picture like this...

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:16.970
Just from memory, I can
tell you about over 250 VIPs,

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.970
celebrities whose scandals he's uncovered, in 42 countries worldwide.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.430
Many of his pictures have had serious political and social consequences.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.610
The Royal Family, Mob bosses... There's no picture I can't take.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.110
Six times, it's almost gotten me killed.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.110
I've been sued for character defamation over 100 times.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.990
That just shows how good you are, Lance.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.830
Your usual fee, okay?

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.460
No, I'd like double.

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.830
Actually, Chief Editor,

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:55.470
I've decided that it'll be my last picture before I throw away my camera.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:56.760
Throw away his camera?

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.840
So he's going to retire?

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:00.800
Lance!

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:06.770
I'm sick of it.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.810
I've been chasing celebrities for over 20 years. I'm done.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.190
My curiosity's been sated, too.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.700
Stop trying to bluff, Victor Lance.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.700
What?

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.490
I've known you for many years.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:30.710
I'm sure you know that your scoops have been declining in both quality and amount over the past few years.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.920
That's because there's nobody worth chasing anymore.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.680
I see...

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:48.430
Why don't you go out with a bang that'll surprise the whole world, then?

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.020
What do you mean?

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.440
Is there somebody else whose picture you want?

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:58.320
No, forget it, Lance.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.450
Even you couldn't...

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.200
Wh-Who is it?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.960
From the way you're talking, it must be some big shot!

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:12.040
I'll admit that you're extremely skilled.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.460
But he's too dangerous.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.420
I said, who is he?

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.420
Sir...

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:28.980
Th-That's... Golgo 13!

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.310
Th-That's... Golgo 13!

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.480
Th-That's... Golgo 13!

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.230
A sniper who kills for money.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:43.490
An A+ class sniper who completes any job, no matter how dangerous.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:50.000
There would be no greater scoop in the world than a picture of him the moment he shoots.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.750
The moment he shoots.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:52.790
Yes.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:58.050
No photographer has ever taken a photo of him firing.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:04.300
If you could capture it, you would go down in history as a legendary photographer.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:06.970
But...

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.470
But?

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:13.940
He won't let anyone who sees him fire live.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.980
That's why he's dangerous.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.480
That sounds fun.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.110
<i>Perfect.</i>

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:23.280
<i>He's a worthy rival for me to hang my retirement on.</i>

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.070
Golgo 13...

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:47.260
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:58.610
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:10.370
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:16.670
The weak person I was is no more

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:22.260
I decided to just believe

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:29.390
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:33.220
I go towards you

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:40.940
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:45.070
I go towards you

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:49.120
Blown by the wind

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:54.580
Oh blown

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.500
Cross Angle

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.510
You got Golgo 13's schedule?

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.430
I know a good information broker

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:14.020
who can even hack into the Department of Defense's most classified servers.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.730
You pulled the information out of the Pentagon?

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:21.480
He got a little spooked the second he heard the name of the guy I was looking for, though.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:25.690
Makes sense, considering your target.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:29.990
Snipers and photographers are basically the same, Patrick.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:35.660
They find the best position,
wait for their chance, and then...

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:37.500
Shoot!

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.460
They just use different tools.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.500
I see.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:49.010
In other words, since I've gone after the same prey for so many years, I know what he'll do.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.470
I'm going to win this game.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.470
I'm counting on you, Lance.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:07:01.810
If "One shot, one kill" is his style, then I'm only going to take one photo on this job.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.360
Just one?

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:09.030
I'll capture the second when he pulls the trigger and the barrel flashes.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:19.410
And that one picture will make the name "Victor Lance" a legend!

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:46.150
This is the building complex where the target's hideout is.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.570
If I was going to go after him, I'd...

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.760
That's it...

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:18.260
And this is the best position to see him.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:25.270
Now, I just wait for the target and Golgo 13.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:39.040
Here he is!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:58.260
Now, show up, Golgo 13!

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:04.390
Why isn't he showing up?

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:06.810
It can't be...

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.820
It's Lance.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:18.200
That schedule of Golgo 13's you got me... It can't be a fake, can it?

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.530
If you don't believe me, I'm hanging up.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.040
Impossible...

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:32.960
Th-Then where did he-

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.420
Th-Then where did he-

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:40.600
Impossible!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.390
From a place like that?

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:57.110
From a tossing boat?

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:02.910
I never thought he would strike from a place even you couldn't predict... What a monster!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.830
A monster?

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.410
You're saying I can't get him 'cause he's a monster?

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:10.670
Next time!

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:12.630
Next time, it's for real!

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.630
You're going to keep doing it?

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:17.170
There's <i>nothing</i>!

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:20.140
There's <i>nothing</i> I can't photograph!

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.520
L-Lance?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:31.360
<i>I might have made a huge mistake in giving him that idea...</i>

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:46.200
I've known you for years!

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.660
Why don't you get it?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:50.250
You're going after Golgo 13!

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.330
Please!

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:53.090
Just one more time!

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:57.420
I need the information from you... Please, please!

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:58.590
Come on!

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.930
I've found his next job.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.480
It's in London.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:23.620
I hacked into the computer of the agent who hired him and found the target's code name.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.620
The target is an arms merchant named "Bishop."

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:34.170
I don't know where he is now, but he'll be returning to his hideout in London by tomorrow afternoon.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.710
Where's his hideout?

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:37.960
Belic Road?

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.220
Okay, got it.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:44.470
Lance, I'm warning you.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.310
You need to stop this.

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.470
If he finds out, you're done for!

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.770
I don't want to get any more involved.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.730
This is my last call.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:53.770
Yeah.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.480
You're a fool.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:59.690
You're insane!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.340
<i>Just wait, Golgo 13.</i>

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:28.220
<i>I'm going to win this fight, and become a legend!</i>

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.190
<i>I'm sure of it.</i>

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:25.320
<i>The top floor of that building is the target's hideout.</i>

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:30.830
Go around that building.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:34.410
Jeez... It's not even that nice of a building.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:40.340
I don't understand why my client asked me to design one just like it.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:14:00.860
<i>You could hit the target even from this hotel, but if he was further back in the room, it'd be impossible.</i>

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.530
<i>With a possible firing angle of 98 degrees,</i>

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:13.120
<i>and an effective firing range of 2500 feet, Golgo 13 can only complete his mission under these conditions.</i>

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:18.120
<i>The problem is what point inside this cone he'll pick.</i>

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:22.130
<i>For example, the Lead Hotel is ideal for a sniper.</i>

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.630
<i>But which window will he aim from?</i>

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:30.300
<i>If I can't predict that, I can't set my camera.</i>

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.560
<i>No, wait...</i>

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:38.140
<i>If I make it so he can't aim from any window...</i>

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:44.480
<i>Okay, that halves it to 49 degrees.</i>

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:48.150
<i>This is the only place he could aim from.</i>

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.860
<i>The emergency exit stairs of the Adelu House.</i>

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.870
<i>This is it.</i>

00:14:54.830 --> 00:15:00.250
<i>And now that I know where he's sniping from, I just need to pick my spot.</i>

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:06.380
He won't let anyone who takes a photo of him live.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:11.800
<i>A point where I can see and photograph him from, but he can't see me.</i>

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:12.890
<i>A place like that...</i>

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.440
<i>Of course.</i>

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.900
<i>There'd be no such thing.</i>

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.780
<i>No, there's gotta be some way.</i>

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.900
<i>Some way of keeping him from noticing when I take his picture.</i>

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.410
<i>I know!</i>

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:37.910
<i>I can do that!</i>

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:45.920
<i>Now the game is truly mine!</i>

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.330
<i>This is the best angle.</i>

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:08.130
<i>Let's get started.</i>

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:16.930
Is this the Lead Hotel?

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.770
I've put something interesting in your hotel.

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:25.350
<i>Now, fall for my trap, Golgo 13!</i>

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:41.660
Sir, sir!

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:42.700
Sir, sir!

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:50.710
I'm sorry to disturb your rest.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:55.380
We're asking all of our guests to evacuate.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:57.380
Why?

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:03.390
We received a phone call saying that a bomb has been planted in this building.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.390
We'd like you to leave immediately.

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:10.020
Listen to the policeman!

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.270
Come this way!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.490
Wait!

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:26.250
<i>Just like I thought, he was going to aim for the Lead Hotel.</i>

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:30.420
<i>Now he's only got one sniping point left!</i>

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:45.310
<i>What are you doing, Golgo 13?</i>

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:48.230
<i>It's almost time for the target to get here!</i>

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.690
<i>There he is.</i>

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.280
<i>It's the target!</i>

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:59.950
<i>Now come, Golgo 13.</i>

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:01.870
<i>I'm ready whenever!</i>

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:35.230
<i>What's wrong, Golgo 13?</i>

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.480
<i>Why don't you show up?</i>

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:53.790
<i>H-He's here!</i>

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.000
<i>H-He's here!</i>

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:10.180
Pigeons?

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:18.230
<i>I win, Golgo 13!</i>

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:22.070
<i>It looks like the time has come for a photo of you firing!</i>

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:29.700
<i>He's mine!</i>

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:56.900
<i>I've been done in.</i>

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:58.150
<i>Damn!</i>

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:02.490
<i>But why? How did he know I was pointing my camera at him?</i>

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.660
<i>I see...</i>

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.580
<i>The light from the sun reflected off my camera lens...</i>

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:18.840
<i>To be able to watch the surrounding area so carefully when he's firing...</i>

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:20.090
<i>What a monster!</i>

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:24.090
<i>He<i> is a monster.</i></i>

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:29.760
Patrick.

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.600
I lost, totally.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:37.480
Yeah, let's have a drink when I get back.

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:39.650
To celebrate my failure to become a legend.

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:00.000
<i>I get it!</i>

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:06.170
<i>He even knew that the target would open his curtains to look at the 12:00 news on that electronic ticker,</i>

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:08.640
<i>and he was waiting for that.</i>

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:11.970
What a terrifying man!

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:22.150
<i>A-A perfectionist monster...</i>

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:23.820
<i>A-A perfectionist monster...</i>

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:26.740
<i>Golgo 13!</i>

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:38.960
It doesn't matter anymore

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:44.460
Who craved freedom first

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:53.390
How we decided to part, and how we loved each other

00:22:53.390 --> 00:22:55.680
As nostalgic and simply just that

00:22:55.720 --> 00:23:03.770
Once you've lost it you'll feel lonely

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:07.610
You may have to overcome the pain

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:12.910
Many times with that cruel heart of yours

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:21.210
But you just can't become as strong as you've imagined

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.750
It was just a dream

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:29.130
So let us return to tomorrow

00:23:29.170 --> 00:23:34.180
In this calm night

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:36.350
There'll only be wanderers

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:41.480
But now you've awakened, so walk down that path of yours

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:47.480
And even though time is fleeting

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:53.990
People sometimes desire too much

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:05.840
Golgo meets a man on an infiltration mission...

00:24:06.340 --> 00:24:09.130
Code name: Ax-3.

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:11.050
His target was the same as Golgo's.

00:24:11.050 --> 00:24:13.050
He was a first-class sniper.

00:24:14.090 --> 00:24:20.180
When the mission is complete,
the fate of professionals awaits them.

00:24:20.180 --> 00:24:22.390
Next time, on Golgo 13:

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:25.810
Deadly Shadow of the Setting Sun

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:24.400
Deadly Shadow of the Setting Sun.

00:24:24.400 --> 00:24:28.610
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
